“New” Cohorts (can be found in [datahub schema|https://datahub.data.boltint.net/dataset/urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:glue,feature_models_spark.feature_micromobility_user_date_utc_lifecycle_frequency_segmentation,PROD)/Schema?is_lineage_mode=false&schemaFilter=] and [datahub documentation|https://datahub.data.boltint.net/dataset/urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:glue,feature_models_spark.feature_micromobility_user_date_utc_lifecycle_frequency_segmentation,PROD)/Documentation?is_lineage_mode=false]). 

Definitions:

!image-20250729-071928.png|width=1446,height=587,alt="image-20250729-071928.png"!

4a. Lifecycle Segmentation (categorized by ride recency):

* zero_activity: users who have never taken a MM ride;
* churned: users without any MM rides within the past 84 days;
* churning: users without any MM rides within the past 42 days but with 1+ MM rides between 42 and 84 days ago;
* new: users whose 1st MM ride was completed within the past 28 days;
* active: not new users who have 1+ MM rides within the past 42 days.


4b. Activity Segmentation (categorized by ride frequency relative to overall city activity), applicable to New and Active users:

* spontaneous: users [whose normalised average weekly rides are <=10%] OR [whose normalised average monthly rides are <=7.5%];
* low_frequency: users [whose normalised average weekly rides are >10% but <=20%] OR [whose normalised average monthly rides are >7.5% but <=17.5%];
* medium_high_frequency: users [whose normalised average weekly rides are >20%] OR [whose normalised average monthly rides are >17.5%].

