Hello, [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949].

Thank you for your request.
Under the Article 15 of the GDPR, the scooter rider (as a data subject) has the right to access personal data processed about them. This includes driving data that can be linked to the rider, such as:

* Driving logs;
* Battery status at the time of the ride;
* Braking system data;
* Error messages generated during the ride;
* Vehicle (scooter) ID if it is linked to their user account.

The information about the broken spring in the brake assembly is not personal data. It is technical / operational information about the scooter, not about the user themselves.

Given the above and as I see the situation, we are legally required to provide the rider with any personal data linked to their ride / their account under the Article 15 of the GDPR. However, we are not required to share technical / mechanical diagnostics (like the broken spring) as it is not considered personal data. Doing so and in this way providing excessive information may expose us to liability and is not required under GDPR. In any case, it is recommended to preserve all logs and ensure no data is altered, to protect against manipulation allegations and to ensure being able to provide such data, if reasonably required in the future.

However, taking into account that this question is connection with the GDPR related matters, I also kindly advise to double check this with our privacy / data protection team, e.g. [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd].

Thank you.

* “*_Switch off automatic blocks for Captive Fleet drivers_*” - within the product request, a caveat should be enabled as to allow Bolt to be a overide any fleet owner controls in case of force majeur events, i.e. police informs us that the driver has kidnapped someone - Bolt should retain the power to block the driver for security purposes. 
{color:#bf2600}Added to doc{color}

* “*_Block all Captive Fleet drivers from bonuses_*” - it is agreed that branding is not considered a bonus, however we would like to discuss the branding compensation here. Could you confirm the following:
** Will the fleet owner be the owner of the cars used by the employee drivers?
{color:#bf2600}It’s unclear exactly but likely the Fleet will be either owner of the car or it’s lease, either way these are cars that will be provided by the empoyer and not by the employee.{color}
** Will all or some cars be branded?
{color:#bf2600}All cars will be branded{color}
** If yes to both, to be considered whether a product change is required to enable a branding commission to the fleet owner which is based on the number of rides completed by the vehicule and not by the driver.
Cars will be branded, but will not enter in the Branded scheme.


* “*_Remove driver support chat from their app_*” - same as above, a caveat should be enabled to allow drivers to contact driver support for emergency and security reasons. {color:#bf2600}Added to doc{color}

